{
  "format": "spreadsheet-app",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "3D Print Quote & Actual Cost Tracker",
  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "Quote desk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "Quote summary",
          "source": "# 3D-print quote desk\n\nEstimate material, electricity, machine wear, finishing labor, and a failure allowance. The quote price adds the editable markup. **Accept and save quote** records the current inputs and totals as values, so future rate changes do not rewrite an accepted price.\n\nThe example quote is for a small PETG cable guide. Try raising **PrintHours** from 3.5 to 5; energy, wear, failure allowance, and quote price update together. Accept it to add a frozen record to **Quote records**."
        },
        {
          "type": "script",
          "name": "Cost function",
          "source": "PrintCost(material, energy, wear, labor) = material + energy + wear + labor"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "name": "RateCard",
          "rowCount": 6,
          "colCount": 2,
          "cells": [
