        {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "Actual cost review",
          "source": "# Actual cost review\n\nCompleted jobs use current material and machine rates to estimate their direct cost. Compare that cost with the estimate frozen when the customer accepted the quote. A positive difference means the job cost more than expected.\n\n{% let over = COUNTIF(CompletedJobs[Difference], \">0\") %}\n**{{ over }}** seeded jobs exceeded their original direct-cost estimate. The failed calibration print is included in actual grams and print hours; keep failed attempts in the job record so their cost does not disappear."
        },
